Chris waters here with a gamespot news  update during the latest Weekend Update  for destiny Bungie responded to an  accusation that they're ignoring Xbox  users a fan asked will you guys give a  nod to your Xbox fan base or just keep  ignoring them Bungie community manager  David dig responded with who's ignoring  you we're right here making a game we  hope you'll love we're listening to your  questions and answering the ones we can  if you're a gamer who wants to play a  bungie game you're very much on our mind  every day on that's sweet the fans  question is likely derived from the fact  that destiny was featured at Sony's  PlayStation 4 announcement in February's  2013 and then again at Sony's e3  briefing later that year furthermore  sony has teamed up with bungie for a new  ps4 commercial and perhaps most  importantly the destiny beta is coming  this summer first to PlayStation 3 and 4  Bungie of course is famous for the Halo  games which were originally released  exclusively for Xbox consoles so this  seeming change of loyalty is notable  however timed exclusivity for specific  platform is nothing new with  multi-platform games just look at all  the call of duty DLC for the last  generation that came first to xbox 360  it's less about what the developers  prefer as a platform and more about the  business side of things we've got a  bunch of new gameplay footage for  destiny up on the site right now as well  as a hefty preview so be sure to check  that out and stay tuned to gamespot com  all this week for continuing destiny  coverage
 

